2. layers/easylist/canonical-keys.txt — MODIFIED VERSION OF EASYLIST

   MODIFICATION NOTICE (GPLv3 section 5(a)): this file is a modified
   version of EasyList, produced by 1Blocker on 2026-11-25 from the
   exact snapshot identified above (canonicalizer version
   v3).

   Nature of the modification: EasyList's network-blocking rules have
   been translated into exact-match URL keys — one `host` or
   `host/path` per line — for Apple's NEURLFilter system (on-device
   Bloom prefilter + private-information-retrieval lookup). The policy
   is to choose keys that match only URLs their source rules would
   block. A key for a directory rule ending in a slash can also match
   the path without that slash. The system applies keys across apps
   and request types, including top-level navigations. An allowlist
   exception that exempts a whole page is honored only for requests to
   that page itself; requests made from that page can still be blocked.
   Cosmetic and scriptlet rules, blocking rules with `$` options,
   and regex and unanchored patterns are omitted. Some rules limited
   by allowlist exceptions are also omitted. Substantial parts of
   EasyList are therefore not represented in this file, and it is not a
   general-purpose filter list.

