4. BLOOM PREFILTER AND CORRESPONDING SOURCE

   The Bloom prefilter for Apple's NEURLFilter system is a bit vector.
   The included builder's bloombuilder command produced it from every
   key in the canonical key file and every key in the mandatory key
   file of this release, and from nothing else. The build document
   listed in section 3 records the inputs, the parameters and the
   expected output identity.

   The public release carries the vector as prefilter.bloom.
   1Blocker conveys the vector in object-code form under the
   GNU General Public License version 3 or (at your option) any later
   version, by offering access from a designated place (GPLv3
   section 6(d)).

   The complete corresponding source is offered at no charge as
   payload.aar in the immutable public release at
   https://github.com/1Blocker/URLFilters/releases/tag/v20261127T052309Z

   The source archive contains both key files, the upstream mirror,
   the license texts, the build document, the builder and this notice.
   In the public release, legal-notice.txt contains this notice,
   followed by the builder's license and the license texts listed in
   section 3.

   While this release is current on the CloudKit record that serves
   devices, that record carries the vector in its "prefilterVector"
   asset, offers the same source archive at no charge in its "archive"
   asset, and carries the same legal notice in its "legalNotice" asset.

